Z||000002||Old Lar||07-13-2000||07:01 AM||||The Fiero Connection was a magazine from FOA (Fiero Owners of America). They put out a nice magazine, however I think it folded into FOCOA and the editor is on the board of FOCOA.<P>When I did belong, I too got only half the issues promised.  Many of these clubs rely on input from Fiero owners for articles, information and photos. Not much input goes out and they have difficulties publishing.   The expense of producing a nice magazine is quit high.||||reg||3
Z||000003||Philphine||07-13-2000||09:53 AM||||thats one reason why i was trying to generate interest in contacting and concentrating on one of the more major car mags. sport compact car at that time. with the number of people on this forum we wouldn't take a magazine over but hopefully we could get one thinking about us. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||07-13-2000||10:16 AM||||I use to be a member of FOA then they went to the new Fiero Connection magazine. I think I got the first full year then 1/2 of the second year. When I wrote and asked about them they refunded my membership fee and told me thay wanted me to sign up as a "lifetime" member. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||HarryG||07-13-2000||12:46 PM||||Philphine,<P>Saw your comments about getting major car magazines thinking about us.<P>Do you mean coverage of events or individual car features?<P>Harry<P> ||||reg||5
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||07-13-2000||02:13 PM||||I think I have either been out of touch or maybe someone was paying attention to us...Fieros West started in 1987 and since then our newsletter (never to be confused with a magazine) has been called Fiero Connection. :O As for FOCOA, there are only 2 people who comprise the Fiero Owner's Club of America and that is Gloria and Phil. There is noone else putting together the magazine, putting on the National Fiero shows, or running the mail order service. Just them. (eek!) They work hard for what they do.<P>As I understand it they had been having disagreements with FOA due to the similarities in names.||||reg||11
Z||000007||Boodoggin||07-13-2000||02:56 PM||||philphine- Good idea about the magazines.  I am also going to contact horsepower tv some time and tell them to do a fiero build up.  Ive seen them do almost anything else like work on astrovans, a 90 trans am, and even civic. Why not a fiero?? It would be cool.  I think it would be cool to see them do a northstar or v8 swap.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Boodoggin (edited 07-13-2000).]||||reg||3
